From da2eff13668d452595df007bd6ef8959f10608d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:05:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Retire reviewer model-diversity admission and
 reroute gates

Model equality and absent author-model attribution are not review failures.
Keep genuine separate reviewer run/session custody, exact artifact/PR/SHA
approval, required CI, route eligibility, mandatory pins and actual quota/pacing.
The runtime resolver and wall/pace/offer consumers must not reserve author models.
Retain historical attribution collectors without using them as routing exclusions.

Why-chain: obsolete provenance/runbook guidance and enforcing code were treated as
current user policy. Earlier author-epoch/artifact narrowing corrected history
sets but retained the criterion. Tests asserted diversity refusals rather than
conformance with the user's retirement. Remove that criterion at all consumers;
keep unavailable-pool, registry and lifecycle negative controls. The canonical
state ship validator is corrected separately under the same task.

Proof: new tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_review_model_retirement.py demonstrated
8 RED failures on the old runtime and 8 GREEN after criterion removal. Consumer
fixtures now test author-model positives and actual provider holds instead of
mistaking authorship for route unavailability. Legacy no-policy class/profile
allocation remains available without model-provenance requirements.

Owner: t_2cfd929843a880df. Same-model review is permitted; a genuine independent
execution, exact-head verdict and CI remain mandatory before canonical shipping.
